# Welcome to mdxx ~title

## Section 1: Content ~section1

This is Section 1 -- where your content lives. It's just standard
Markdown. Write headings, paragraphs, lists, images, tables -- anything
you'd normally write in a `.md` file.

The only additions are:

- **ID tags** like `~title` at the end of a line -- these let Section 2
  style that element
- **Comment anchors** like {{c1}}this highlighted phrase{{/c1}} -- these
  attach review comments defined in Section 2
- **Inline spans** like [this text]{~highlight} -- these style a range
  of text within a paragraph
~features-list

That's it. Section 1 stays clean and readable.

## Section 2: Styling ~section2

Below the first `----------------------------------------` divider is
Section 2. It holds all the visual styling: fonts, colors, sizes,
page layout, headers, footers, and comment definitions.

You never put styling in Section 1, and you never put content in
Section 2.

## Section 3: Agent Instructions ~section3

Below the second divider is Section 3. This section is for LLMs and
agents that edit the document. It tells them the rules: naming
conventions, constraints, what not to touch.

The renderer ignores Section 3 entirely.

----------------------------------------

@page {
  size: letter;
  margin: 1in;
}

@defaults {
  font-family: "Inter";
  font-size: 11pt;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  line-height: 1.6;
  heading-font-family: "Inter";
  heading-1-size: 26pt;
  heading-2-size: 20pt;
}

@title {
  font-size: 28pt;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 8pt;
}

@section1 {
  font-size: 18pt;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: #0066cc;
}

@section2 {
  font-size: 18pt;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: #0066cc;
}

@section3 {
  font-size: 18pt;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: #0066cc;
}

@features-list {
  item-spacing: 6pt;
}

@highlight {
  color: #0066cc;
  font-weight: 700;
  background: #e6f0ff;
}

@comment:c1 {
  author: "Example";
  date: "2026-04-04";
  text: "This is a comment attached to the highlighted phrase above.";
  resolved: false;
}

----------------------------------------

# mdxx Agent Guide

## Rules
- Section 1 is standard Markdown. Keep it human-readable.
- Only add ~id tags to elements that need custom styling.
- Use lowercase-kebab-case for IDs.
- Comment anchors: {{id}}...{{/id}}
- Inline spans: [text]{~id}
- Never put styling in Section 1. Never put content in Section 2.

## Constraints
- This is an introductory example document.
- Keep the tone simple and explanatory.
